# Deployment, CI, operations

Primary references:

- `docs/implementation/technology_baseline.md`
- `docs/implementation/agent_reference_index.md`
- active implementation deployment/operations group plan.

Rules:

- deployment-specific versions/runtime/capabilities are pinned and verified, not assumed from generic vendor capability;
- prefer workload identity/federation and service principals for automation; do not introduce long-lived secrets when a supported federation path exists;
- keep environment configuration explicit/versioned and prevent cross-environment accidental writes;
- deployment rollback must not rewrite canonical semantic history;
- platform/integration/reasoning/control health dimensions remain distinct from monitored-domain health;
- SLOs are service-class/deployment specific, not one global health score;
- quota/backpressure/capacity failures degrade service/coverage explicitly and do not manufacture domain negatives;
- cost policy cannot silently weaken evidence retention/control promises;
- backup/restore/DR exercises must preserve explicit gaps and historical non-rewriting semantics;
- optional integration outage should degrade only dependent capabilities.
